    "created_at": "2021-10-06T04:44:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-06T05:24:34Z",
    "body": "Most of these are certainly part of the specs language, see https://infra.spec.whatwg.org\r\n\r\nIn particular,\r\n- a term surrounded by double quotes in a monospace font [denotes a string](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string);\r\n- backticks denote [Byte sequences](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#byte-sequences);\r\n- [guillemets denote lists](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lists), but in this particular case, `«[ ]»` [denotes a Map](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#maps).\r\n\r\nAlso, CSS values and properties (like [`'overflow'`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#'overflow')) are surrounded by single quotes, some may have other meanings too, but the case you exposed seems to be a direct quotation from a [W3C text](https://www.w3.org/TR/charmod/#abstract).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
